# Complete semantic translation of the historical standalone usbser.wlcmd.
#
# Native locklint automatically recognizes 19 of the 21 historical explicit
# roots and all four dev_ops targets through external linkage or escaped
# function pointers.  The remaining usbser_cpr_suspend and usbser_cpr_resume
# functions are reached by resolved calls from the rooted detach and attach
# entry points.  Native also recognizes usbser_restart and the
# recovery-sequence functions as escaped callbacks.
#
# OSLL produces identical protected-access findings with and without
# "one usbser_state".  Native locklint distinguishes concrete object
# identities and needs no equivalent declaration for this focused module.
#
# The historical 24 ds_ops targets pointed at warlock_dummy.  Native locklint
# retains those external device-specific calls as indirect rather than
# inventing implementations.  The mutable rseq_step table likewise retains
# indirect calls, while its in-module target functions remain automatic roots.
#
# The historical bus_ops mappings cannot affect usbser because neither module
# translation unit calls through bus_ops.
#
# OSLL anchors the multiline port_lh assignment at line 848 while native
# Sparse anchors it at line 846.  OSLL also reports adjacent port_state reads
# at lines 943 and 944; Sparse reuses the line-943 load.  The runner normalizes
# only those accepted differences before comparing exact source/member pairs.
